---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services | OpsDevCode"
  description="Outcome-driven platform work: health checks, FinOps, IaC, CI/CD, Kubernetes, custom tooling, architecture review, fractional advice, agentic workflows."
>
  <Header active="Services" />
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="section" id="services">
        <h2 class="section-title">What I do</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-2col">
            <div class="tile" id="platform-health">
              <h3>Platform Health Check</h3>
              <p>Identify bottlenecks, risks, and unnecessary complexity in your platform, with clear next steps to improve it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>FinOps</h3>
              <p>Reduce cloud spend and improve visibility into where your infrastructure budget is going.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>IaC</h3>
              <p>Clean up and standardize infrastructure as code so your team can move faster with less risk.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>CI/CD</h3>
              <p>Improve delivery speed and reliability with simpler pipelines your team can actually maintain.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>Kubernetes</h3>
              <p>Operate K8s and the surrounding platform with predictable upgrades, scaling, and day-two behavior — not surprises.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>Custom tooling</h3>
              <p>Build lightweight internal tools that remove friction and automate repetitive work.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>Architecture Review</h3>
              <p>Stress-test big bets before you commit — networking, clusters, and how changes reach production.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>Fractional Platform Advisor</h3>
              <p>Senior platform judgment on a fixed cadence — strategy, vendors, and team direction without a full-time hire.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3><a href="/agentic" style="color: inherit">Agentic Development</a></h3>
              <p>Explore practical agent-based workflows that improve developer and operational efficiency.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="how">
        <h2 class="section-title">How we'll work together</h2>
          <div class="steps-row">
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>1) Quick intro (15 min)</h3>
              <p>We talk through what's going on and what you're hoping for. If it's not a good fit, I'll tell you straight up.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>2) I take a look</h3>
              <p>Usually read-only access — billing, K8s, your IaC repos. I try not to get in your team's way.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>3) You get a plan</h3>
              <p>Prioritized: quick wins first, then medium fixes, then the bigger structural stuff.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile">
              <h3>4) We fix it</h3>
              <p>I implement or pair with your team. Most of my work is async and time-boxed — no endless retainer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="note" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            If you're about to hire a "Senior DevOps / Platform / SRE" because things are a mess,
            this is often a faster way to get stable first — before you add headcount.
          </div>
      </section>

      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-32);">
        <a class="btn primary" href="https://calendly.com/eric-opsdevco/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a discovery call</a>
      </p>

      <Footer />
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
